colspan="3" align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1">Weighted cost of ambulance transportation</td><td align="center" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">188.06</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td colspan="3" align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1"><bold>Average cost of a hospital-treated exacerbation</bold></td><td align="center" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>1,346.63</bold></td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tfn22-copd-7-183"><p><bold>Notes:</bold></p></fn><fn id="tfn23-copd-7-183"><label>a</label><p>Calculated according to the formula: [(sum_activity units &#x000d7; sum_national average unit cost)<sub>LONG STAY</sub> + (sum_activity units &#x000d7; sum_national average unit cost)<sub>SHORT STAY</sub>]/[(sum_activity units)<sub>LONG STAY</sub> + (sum_activity units)<sub>SHORT STAY</sub>]. Source:<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b23-copd-7-183">23</xref>;</p></fn><fn id="tfn24-copd-7-183"><label>b</label><p>the cost of ambulance transportation was estimated at &#x000a3;208.95 based on the National Schedule of Reference Costs Year: &#x02018;2009/10&#x02019; - NHS trusts paramedic services: category B/Amber, service code PS06B (06 breathing problems; breathing difficulty). It was assumed that 90% of patients would be delivered to hospital by ambulance.<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b23-copd-7-183">23</xref></p></fn><fn id="tfn25-copd-7-183"><p><bold>Abbreviations:</bold> NHS, National Health Service; HRG, Healthcare Resource Group; COPD, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease; NIV, Non-invasive ventilation; GBP, British pound; CC, complications and co-morbidities.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></app></app-group><ref-list><title>References</title><ref id="b1-copd-7-183"><label>1</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Buist</surname><given-names>AS</given-names></name><name><surname>Vollmer